<title>MEXICO: Cintra elects board, creates reserves.</title>
<headline>Cintra elects board, creates reserves.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Cintra SA on Wednesday said it elected a new board of directors during a shareholders' meeting and approved the creation of reserves to buy outstanding shares.</p>
<p>Cintra, the holding company for Mexicana and Aeromexico airlines, did not specify the amount of reserves it intended to create.</p>
<p>Ernesto Martens was elected as president, while several board members of Mexican banks were also elected to the board of Cintra, including Carlos Gomez y Gomez of Grupo Financiero Invermexico and Adolfo Lagos, head of Grupo Financiero Serfin.</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom, +525 728-9565))</p>
